    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "it's just that the more i think about it, the more it feels like it's all just math. if life has no inherent meaning, then staying alive or not staying alive are just two different variables. they both end up at zero eventually. so why is one more \"correct\" than the other? it feels like people just pretend there's a difference because they're scared of the logic.",
